  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Elimination Partnership in the Indo-Pacific for Cervical Cancer (EPICC)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EPICC will deliver cervical cancer control activities (HPV immunisation, screening and treatment) in line with WHO&apos;s global strategy for the elimination of cervical cancer. EPICC sets out a four-tiered country approach to identifying and meeting policy objectives essential to the development of sustainable cervical cancer control programs.

EPICC brings together a consortium of leading Australian cancer research and implementation partners with Ministries of Health in the Indo-Pacific region to advance their national cervical cancer elimination strategies. 

Partner countries (PNG, Malaysia, Timor-Leste, Solomon Islands, Vanuatu, Tuvalu, Fiji and Nauru) are tiered according to readiness, gaps and priorities. The total value of this investment is $16.5 million over 4 years, starting FY2023-24.</narrative>
  </description>
